      "math_academy_id": "q-49097",
      "knowledge_point_id": "cf98ee24-7774-5674-8a1e-63f4f6d225c0",
      "knowledge_point": "Integrating a Reciprocal Function",
      "problem": "Calculate $\\int \\frac{\\text{d}x}{9x}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we apply the constant factor rule and take the coefficient $\\frac{1}{9}$ out of the integral. Then we compute the integral of $\\frac{1}{x},$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}x}{9x} & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}ln⁡|x|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{1}{9}ln⁡|x|+C"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "ln⁡(9+x)+C"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
