    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-103374",
      "knowledge_point_id": "3c865ec2-5bed-5892-966b-a586097be923",
      "knowledge_point": "Integrating the Sum of a Reciprocal Function and a Power Function",
      "problem": "Calculate $\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}-6}{2x}\\,dx.$",
      "worked_solution": "Applying the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}-6}{2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2x}-\\frac{3}{x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{3}{2}x-\\frac{3}{x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\int x\\,\\text{d}x-3\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{2}-3ln⁡|x|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
