    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-49100",
      "knowledge_point_id": "3c865ec2-5bed-5892-966b-a586097be923",
      "knowledge_point": "Integrating the Sum of a Reciprocal Function and a Power Function",
      "problem": "Find the integral of ${(2-\\frac{1}{x})}^{2}$ with respect to $x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Expanding the binomial and applying the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {(2-\\frac{1}{x})}^{2}\\text{d}x & =\\int (4-\\frac{4}{x}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int 4\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{4}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\int \\text{d}x-4\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4x-4ln⁡|x|+\\frac{{x}^{-2+1}}{-2+1}+C \\\\  & =4x-4ln⁡|x|-\\frac{1}{x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
